              "id": "python/DjangoUnvalidatedPassword",
              "name": "DjangoUnvalidatedPassword",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Password Requirements Not Enforced in Django Application"
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "\n## Details\n\nDjango applications allow the developer to configure password policies that\nensure users provide reasonably secure passwords.\n\nIn custom forms, the developer is able to call `User.set_password()` directly on\nuser input, which allows users to provide passwords that may not meet the\napplication requirements.\n\n## Best practises for prevention\n\n* When implementing custom password setting forms, first call\n  `django.shortcuts.validate_password()` on user input before calling\n  `set_password()` on it.",
                "text": ""
              },
